{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 RCA / legitimacy verdict\n\nStep 0(a): searched `reconciler repo root unset fallback cwd independent RuntimeError`, `test_reconciler_repo_root_unset_fallback_is_cwd_independent`, and `_default_repo_root clean wheel cwd not checkout`; no open duplicate found. The related prior ticket is closed `c0b9-33b0-f968-450d` / `impressive-doddering-alpinegoat`.\n\nStep 0(b): reported against scheduled mirror run `33426859481`, event `schedule`, head `8db373933654c7c21fa214565426f562ca55cd80`, created `2026-08-31T18:46:15Z`; suspect-path history since the reported 2026-08-28 window includes `71eef3f56dc5 reconciler: validated layered repo-root fallback` plus unrelated adjacent changes.\n\nStep 0(c): worktree `ci-reconciler-root` is current at `8db373933654c7c21fa214565426f562ca55cd80` (= `origin/main`).\n\nConfirmed mechanism: in a clean non-editable wheel install with `REBAR_ROOT` unset and cwd outside any checkout, `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_reconciler_repo_root_unset_fallback_is_cwd_independent` calls `invariants._default_repo_root()` before arranging any valid package-root or cwd checkout. That reaches `rebar.config.reconciler_repo_root()` step 4 and raises the intended clear `RuntimeError`. Local reproduction from an outside cwd with a built wheel produced the same failure and stack as CI.\n\nLegitimacy verdict: product behavior is correct; the test is over-broad for the clean-install context. Authority: closed bug `c0b9-33b0-f968-450d` acceptance criteria state the intended behavior under a non-editable install is `validated layered fallback, else a clear error naming REBAR_ROOT/--repo-root`. Its landed commit `71eef3f56dc5` documents Option C: `REBAR_ROOT` → validated package root → validated cwd toplevel → clear error; never silently return a non-checkout path. Current `src/rebar/config.py::reconciler_repo_root` carries the same contract in its docstring and implementation, and the adjacent test `test_reconciler_repo_root_errors_when_neither_package_nor_cwd_is_a_checkout` explicitly asserts the raise leg.\n\nAttribution: caused by `c0b9-33b0-f968-450d` as a test-plan escape in the fix that added the over-broad cwd-independence oracle while also defining fail-closed behavior for the no-checkout wheel case. Close class planned: `plan_defect`.\n\nPhase 2 plan: test-only correction. Keep the cwd-independence assertion, but make its precondition explicit by simulating a valid editable/source package-root checkout before changing cwd to an unrelated checkout. The existing adjacent tests continue to cover the clean wheel no-checkout raise leg and the clean wheel cwd-checkout fallback leg. No product code impact; no plan-review gate required."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788218163101664818,"uuid":"1879beb1-156c-4ea6-ad61-1781041dc197"}